ping — one echo a second, answered or timed out

  ping 192.0.2.1         four rounds against an address
  ping gateway.lan       a name; the resolver finds the address
  ping 192.0.2.1 -c 10   a chosen number of rounds

Each round prints the answer and its round trip, or `no answer` after
one second. A summary counts the answered rounds. A name goes through
the hosts file and then DNS; `man resolve` describes that path.

Incoming echoes need no command: the machine answers pings whenever an
interface holds an address, and 127.0.0.1 answers always.
